      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 702562308,
      "version": 222,
      "versionNonce": 380076164,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793289246735,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5. A block needs a slot in ALL four bars at once. Bar 3 is full after\n3, so block 4 can't land anywhere. Result: 3 blocks per SM.\nOccupancy = 3 x 16 = 48 threads seated of 64 = 75%.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5. A block needs a slot in ALL four bars at once. Bar 3 is full after\n3, so block 4 can't land anywhere. Result: 3 blocks per SM.\nOccupancy = 3 x 16 = 48 threads seated of 64 = 75%.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "okjo6UCj7jecLvDMTOoI2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1379.400024045759,
      "y": -194.99999914285706,
      "width": 917.119384765625,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ar",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 627873340,
      "version": 653,
      "versionNonce": 154739332,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793289440650,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Each bar is one pool's whole capacity, cut into slots the size one block needs.\nBlocks land one at a time and take one slot in every bar. The first bar to run out of slots\nstops the landing: the other bars keep their empty slots, unusable. \n\nOccupancy = threads seated / thread seats total, here 48/64 = 75%.\n\nChange the block size or the kernel (more variables = more registers, more shared memory) and\nthe slots resize, so a different bar may fill up first. Smallest slot count always wins.\n\nNsight's occupancies calculator does exactly this with your real card's\nfour limits.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Each bar is one pool's whole capacity, cut into slots the size one block needs.\nBlocks land one at a time and take one slot in every bar. The first bar to run out of slots\nstops the landing: the other bars keep their empty slots, unusable. \n\nOccupancy = threads seated / thread seats total, here 48/64 = 75%.\n\nChange the block size or the kernel (more variables = more registers, more shared memory) and\nthe slots resize, so a different bar may fill up first. Smallest slot count always wins.\n\nNsight's occupancies calculator does exactly this with your real card's\nfour limits.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
